Z||000000||overlord||02-19-2000||08:58 AM||||holy smokes!<P>just came back from work and i have to drive the last 4 miles on gravel.<P>i spied a deer in the corner of my eye and thought "o crap..its gonna runacross the road" and sure enough it started to..so i hit the brakes and actaully fishtaled around it. just barely missing it with the backend of my fiero.  (pause to wipe sweat from forehead)<P>then 30 secs later i came over the top of a hill and seen 5-6 more deer going across the road. i slammmed the brakes, and the wheels locked (i hate it when this happens) and all of the deer were across.....except for one baby that was headin straight for me.<P>i managed to stop and the last deer ran in front of me with only inches to spare.<BR>(pause to check underwear).<P>i thought this was the one for my baby. but i guess someone up there likes her.||||reg||4
Z||000001||2M4 Dale||02-19-2000||10:35 AM||||You gotta remember that if there's one deer that you seen there is about 20 more that you havn't!!!||||reg||1
Z||000002||Monkeyman||02-19-2000||10:59 AM||||They're everywhere!  They're everywhere!  For those of you familiar with the Middletown, Oh area, my wife and I were driving down one of the main streets there over Christmas and I saw a deer walking across the street.  (Keep in mind that this is in the middle of a decent size city)  I kept telling my wife, "Deer!  DEER!  <B>DEER!</B>"  Apparently she thought I meant it like "Honey, Darling, Sweethart".  She finally figured it out in time to swerve and miss the deer by about 6 inches.  Whew!  Good thing it was the middle of the night with little to no traffic!||||reg||1
